    "title": "IDS update problem · New attacks with few labels",
    "notes": "The setting begins with attack labels available at deployment and later receives a few labelled examples of additional attacks. The question is whether the detector can incorporate them while retaining benign and previously labelled attack discrimination. The cited study motivates data scarcity, changing inputs, and error costs; it is not a direct XGBoost–TabPFN comparison.",
