  {
    "title": "Stage-wise detector updates based on the attack collection order",
    "notes": "CIC2018 scheduled different attack types on different collection dates. We retain the order in which those attack types appeared and reveal labelled training rows in that order. We do not sort every row by timestamp, preserve the original time gaps, or replay the complete benign and attack traffic timeline. This is therefore a controlled label-release replay rather than temporal reproduction. ToN-IoT is evaluated independently using its own training split and attack-introduction order.",
