  {
    "title": "Evaluation workflow · Updating a detector with few labels",
    "notes": "CIC2018 begins with 750 benign, 125 Brute force, and 125 DoS rows. DDoS, Web attacks, Infiltration, and Bot are then released with n labelled rows per class. Cumulative retention keeps all released rows, while the fixed buffer removes existing rows and inserts every new row. XGBoost is refitted and TabPFN refreshes its context and cache using the same retained row IDs. Final quality is measured on the same fixed test set, retention on a fixed known-class panel, and update cost after Stage 1 with inference excluded.",
